 "verdict": "RUNG (the unwrapped census reproduces the stored raw census): 6 field-sets compared. Identical, so both arms run the same unmodified estimator and the comparison below is between one estimator and itself, differing only in the model's input domain. STABILITY: 6 of 6 templated censuses agree across both seeds. PRIMARY (same weights, same seeds, only the domain changes): Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct [none] -> [none]; stablelm-zephyr-3b [none] -> [none]; SmolLM2-1.7B-Instruct [funnel] -> [none]  CHANGED; gemma-1.1-2b-it [funnel] -> [none]  CHANGED; Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct [none] -> [none]; Falcon3-3B-Instruct [funnel] -> [funnel]. 2 of 6 models change class under their own chat template. The fixed-point class is DOMAIN-determined, not a property of the weights alone \u2014 2608.10986's BOS effect generalises from one token to a deployment prefix, and F143's null describes the RAW map only. SECONDARY (the within-class quantities the label cannot carry): Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct fix [0.0, 0.0]->[0.0, 0.0] endpoints [7, 14]->[11, 19]; stablelm-zephyr-3b fix [0.0, 0.0]->[0.0208, 0.0] endpoints [3, 5]->[47, 43]; SmolLM2-1.7B-Instruct fix [0.9896, 0.9688]->[0.0104, 0.0104] endpoints [3, 5]->[10, 11]; gemma-1.1-2b-it fix [0.9479, 0.9479]->[0.0, 0.0] endpoints [10, 20]->[16, 13]; Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct fix [0.0, 0.0]->[0.0208, 0.0208] endpoints [33, 36]->[14, 18]; Falcon3-3B-Instruct fix [0.6146, 0.7708]->[0.8438, 0.8333] endpoints [3, 4]->[5, 3]. BOUNDARY: 6 instruction-tuned models, one template each (9-35 prefix tokens), 96 starts, two census seeds. One template is one domain; base models have no template and cannot be run on this axis at all.",
